# object-world
#
# Objects in the world. Finding and grounding objects named by handle (find-object, find-object-direct), 
# anchoring, removing objects, scene/world context and storing objects in semantic memory. Used by tasks that 
# have an object-handle world; the desired-state machinery does not need it.
#
# Requires: soar-base, selection-world, agent-world.
# Loaded by: soar-library.soar
#
# Contents (rules per file)
#     22  find-object-direct.soar: Grounds objects by handle/class directly, including the objects of a relation, selecting as soon as the information is available.
#     22  find-object.soar: Proposes finding an object that a desired needs but that is not grounded yet (known handle, unknown location).
#      5  Impasse__Operator_Tie/evaluate-operator/failed-grounding.soar: In look-ahead, fails an evaluation when grounding fails.
#      1  elaborations/smem-store-in.soar: Stores in-relations in semantic memory.
#      1  elaborations/smem-store-object.soar: Stores objects in semantic memory.
#      1  elaborations/smem-store-scene.soar: Stores scenes in semantic memory.
#      3  elaborations/smem.soar: Cleans up after semantic-memory retrievals.
#      4  elaborations/world-context.soar: World context: classes used to define objects in desireds.
#      1  elaborations/world-from-scene.soar: Builds world objects from the scene.
#      3  find-object/assume-successful-grounding.soar: In look-ahead, assumes a find-object succeeds.
#
# Datamap
#   object-world.vsa.json holds this project's state attributes plus those of the projects it requires.
#   Top-state attributes owned by this project: (none)
#   Single source: datamaps/library-datamap.json (each edge tagged with its owning project). Regenerate the
#   project files with: python3 tools/datamaps.py <this-directory> --assemble
#
# Flags read: smem-store
# Flags written: (none recorded)
# Hooks: not yet defined (see the refactoring proposal, Section 4); this file will list them.
# Conventions: every rule is :default; no rule name is defined twice among the sourced files; do not excise rules to override them.
# Notes: docs/ holds comment-only notes from the old projects (not sourced).

